        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall the curadi root for \"कुण,\" which seems to belong to a group of roots listed together under the meaning \"आमन्त्रणे\" (to invite/address) alongside others like केत, श्राम, गुण.\n\nThe key question is whether कुण is adanta (ending in अ), since that determines whether the final vowel is deleted without guṇa. Recalling the kathādi grouping \"कुण गुण चामन्त्रणे\" alongside गुण (which gives गुणयति), I conclude कुण is also adanta, so the form should be कुणयामः.\n\n",
